hadiths[54]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7078","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Abandoning the bequest is disgrace in this world, and Fire and ignominy in the Hereafter.""**"
"7079","ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""It is not right for a Muslim who has anything to bequeath to pass two dark nights except with his will written beside him.""**"
"7080","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came and announced the death of so-and-so. The Prophet ﷺ asked about his sudden absence, and when told he had just been with them, he ﷺ declared it a seizure taken in divine displeasure, and said: > **""Deprived is he who is deprived of making his will.""**"
"7081","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: they used to open their wills with the testimony that none is worthy of worship but Allah and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger ﷺ, that Paradise is true, Hell is true, the Hour is coming without doubt, and Allah will raise those in the graves. And the testator would enjoin those he left behind with what Ibrāhīm عليه السلام enjoined upon his sons: O my sons, Allah has chosen the religion for you, so die not except as Muslims."
"7082","Ḥanẓalah ibn Ḥudhaym رضي الله عنه reported that his grandfather Ḥanīfah gathered his sons to bequeath one hundred prized camels to an orphan in his care. When his sons intended to honor it in his presence but revoke it after his death, they agreed to take the dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Upon hearing the bequest, the Prophet ﷺ showed anger in his face, rose upon his knees from his sitting, and said: > **""No, no, no. Charity is five, otherwise ten, otherwise fifteen, otherwise twenty, otherwise twenty-five, otherwise thirty, otherwise thirty-five, and if it is much, then forty.""**"
"7083","ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn رضي الله عنه reported that a man freed six of his slaves though he owned nothing else. When his Bedouin heirs informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he ﷺ disapproved of one who leaves his heirs destitute, and said: > **""Has he indeed done that? Had we known, Allah willing, we would not have prayed over him.""**"
"7084","ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn and Samurah ibn Jundub رضي الله عنهما reported that a man freed six slaves at death while owning nothing else. The Prophet ﷺ cast lots among them, saying in effect: > **""Let two be freed and four remain enslaved.""**"
"7085","Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī رضي الله عنه said: a man in his will freed six slaves though he had no wealth besides them. When that reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he ﷺ was angered by exceeding the third, then cast lots and said in effect: > **""Let one-third of them be freed.""**"
"7086","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a man freed six slaves though he had no other wealth, then died. The Prophet ﷺ cast lots among them, and decreed: > **""Let two be freed and four remain enslaved.""**"
"7087","Al-Qāsim said: a man sought his heirs' permission to bequeath more than a third, they permitted him, then retracted it after he died. ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه was asked about it and said: that excess is disapproved and not permissible."
"7088","Al-Qāsim said: Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه was asked about a man who freed his slave at death though he owned nothing else and owed debt. He said: the slave shall work to earn his price for the creditors and heirs."
"7089","Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: beware of depriving heirs throughout life and squandering wealth at death."
"7090","Abū Maysarah ʿAmr ibn Shuraḥbīl al-Hamdānī said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said to me: when one of you notables of Kūfah dies leaving neither paternal heir nor womb-relative, what prevents him from placing his wealth among the poor and needy."
"7091","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has charitably granted you one-third of your wealth at your death.""**"
"7092","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed Allah has charitably granted you one-third of your wealth at your death as an increase in your lifetimes, to make it an increase in your deeds.""**"
"7093","Khālid ibn ʿUbayd al-Sulamī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given you at your death one-third of your wealth as an increase in your deeds.""**"
"7094","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه raised it to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: > **""The Muslim man indeed does good with his third at death, and Allah thereby completes his purification.""**"
"7095","ʿAmr ibn al-Qāriʾ رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Saʿd رضي الله عنه ill when he went to Ḥunayn, then visited him ill and overpowered by pain after returning from al-Jiʿrānah for ʿUmrah. Saʿd asked about bequeathing all his wealth since he had no child to inherit, then two-thirds, then half, and the Prophet ﷺ refused each, until he asked about a third. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Yes, and that is much. I hope Allah will raise you so that some peoples are humbled through you and others benefit through you. O ʿAmr ibn al-Qāriʾ, if Saʿd dies after me here, bury him here.""**"
"7096","ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Makhzūmī from his father from his grandfather reported that Saʿd رضي الله عنه asked the Prophet ﷺ about bequests, and he ﷺ said: > **""A quarter.""**"
"7097","Abū Qatādah رضي الله عنه reported that al-Barāʾ ibn Maʿrūr رضي الله عنه bequeathed one-third of his wealth to the Prophet ﷺ to dispose wherever he wished, but the Prophet ﷺ returned it to his children."
"7098","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that a man bequeathed to another man a share of his wealth, and the Prophet ﷺ fixed it, saying in effect: > **""Let him have a sixth.""**"
"7099","From him رضي الله عنه: a man in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned to another man a share of his wealth, then died without its amount being known. The matter was raised to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ﷺ decreed: > **""Let him have a sixth of his wealth.""**"
"7100","Kaʿb ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, part of my repentance is to detach myself from my wealth and abandon the abode of my people where I committed the sin. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: > **""One-third of that will suffice you.""**"
"7101","Shaddād ibn Aws رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""For you to leave your heirs rich is better than to leave them destitute begging from people. You will not spend any expenditure seeking thereby the Face of Allah but you will be rewarded for it, even what you place in the mouth of your wife.""**"
"7102","Khārijah ibn ʿAmr al-Jumaḥī رضي الله عنه said: on the Day of the Conquest, while I stood by his she-camel, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is no bequest for an heir. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given every rightful one his right, and for the adulterer is deprivation. Whoever claims another than his father or takes as patrons other than his liberators, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; Allah will accept from him neither obligatory nor voluntary deed on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"7103","ʿAlī رضي الله عنه said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""There is no bequest for a killer.""**"
"7104","Hishām ibn ʿUrwah said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, and Muṭīʿ ibn al-Aswad رضي الله عنهم appointed al-Zubayr رضي الله عنه as executor of their wills."
"7105","ʿUrwah said: ʿĀʾishah, Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, Shaybah ibn ʿUthmān, and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir رضي الله عنهم appointed ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr رضي الله عنهما as executor of their wills."
"7106","Abū Ḥuṣayn said: ʿUbaydah bequeathed that al-Aswad should lead his funeral prayer."
"7107","Ṣilah ibn Zufar said: a man of Hamdān came on a piebald horse to ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه and said, my uncle appointed me executor of his estate, and this horse is from it, may I buy it. He said: no, nor shall you borrow anything from his wealth."
"7108","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that near his death the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a sheet to write a document after which they would neither stray nor lead astray. Voices rose in the house and ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه spoke, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set it aside. In another wording he ﷺ intended to write for his Ummah: > **""They shall neither wrong nor be wronged.""**"
"7109","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a shoulder-blade and said: > **""Bring me a shoulder-blade; I shall write for you a document after which you will never differ after me.""**"
"7110","Muʿādh رضي الله عنه said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined me with ten counsels: > **""Associate nothing with Allah, even if you are killed and burned. Do not disobey your parents, even if they command you to leave your family and wealth. Do not deliberately abandon an obligatory prayer, for whoever deliberately abandons an obligatory prayer, the protection of Allah is disavowed from him. Do not drink wine, for it is the head of every obscenity. Beware of disobedience, for by disobedience the wrath of Allah descends. Beware of fleeing from the battlefront, even if people perish; if death befalls people, stand firm. Spend upon your family from your means, do not lift your stick from them in discipline, and make them fear Allah.""**"
"7111","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه was asked by a man for counsel, and replied: you have asked me what I once asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before you. He ﷺ said: > **""I enjoin upon you fear of Allah, for it is the head of everything; upon you is jihād, for it is the monasticism of Islam; upon you is remembrance of Allah and recitation of the Qurʾān, for it is your spirit in the heaven and your remembrance on earth. Guard your tongue except for good, for thereby you will overcome Satan.""**"
"7112","Ḥarmalah al-ʿAnbarī رضي الله عنه said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, O Messenger of Allah, enjoin me. He ﷺ said: > **""Fear Allah. When you sit in a gathering then leave it, and you hear them saying what pleases you, come to it; and when you hear them saying what you dislike, leave it.""**"
"7113","Abū Dharr رضي الله عنه said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, enjoin me. He ﷺ kept increasing me with each asking, enjoining taqwa as the head of the affair, recitation of the Qurʾān and remembrance as light in the heavens and earth, avoiding much laughter which kills the heart and removes the light of the face, jihād as the monasticism of this Ummah, silence except for good which repels Satan and aids the religion, looking to one below and not above so as not to despise Allah's blessing, joining kin even if they sever, fearing no blame in Allah, and loving for people what one loves for oneself. Then he ﷺ struck his hand upon my chest and said: > **""O Abū Dharr, there is no intellect like planning, no piety like restraint, and no nobility like good character.""**"
"7114","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined me with seven traits: > **""Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are cut, burned, or crucified. Do not deliberately abandon prayer, for whoever abandons it deliberately has left the religion. Do not commit disobedience, for it is the wrath of Allah. Do not drink wine, for it is the head of all sins. Do not flee from death, even if you are in it. Do not disobey your parents, even if they command you to leave the entire world, then leave it. Do not put your stick down from your family, and deal justly with them from yourself.""**"
"7115","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined me with seven: > **""Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are cut or burned. Do not deliberately abandon prayer, for whoever abandons it, the protection is disavowed from him. Do not drink wine, for it is the key to every evil. Obey your parents, even if they command you to leave your world, then leave it. Do not dispute authority with its people. Do not flee from the battlefront, even if you perish. Honor your companions, spend upon your family from your means, do not lift the stick from them, and make them fear Allah.""**"
"7116","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه said: my Beloved ﷺ enjoined me: > **""Look to one below you and do not look to one above you. Love the poor and draw near them. Join your womb even if it severs you and treats you harshly. Speak for Allah and fear in Allah no blame of a blamer. Ask no one for anything. And increase in saying: there is no might nor power except through Allah, for it is from the treasures of Paradise.""**"
"7117","Umaymah, freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: I was pouring his ablution water when a man entered and said, enjoin me. He ﷺ said: > **""Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are cut and burned with fire. Do not disobey your parents, even if they command you to abandon your family and world, then abandon it. Do not ever drink wine, for it is the key to every evil. Do not ever deliberately abandon prayer, for whoever does so, the protection of Allah and His Messenger is disavowed from him. Do not ever flee from the battlefront, for whoever does so returns with wrath from Allah and his abode is Hell, an evil destination. Do not ever add to the boundaries of your land, for whoever does so will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying upon his neck the measure of seven earths. Spend upon your family from your means, do not lift your stick from them, and make them fear Allah.""**"
"7118","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined me: > **""Enter the morning of your fast oiled and with combed hair, and do not enter the morning of your fast frowning. Accept the invitation of any Muslim who invites you unless they openly display instruments of music, then do not accept. Pray over whoever dies of the people of our Qiblah, even if executed by crucifixion or stoning. For you to meet Allah with sins nearly filling the earth is better for you than to spread testimony against any of the people of our Qiblah.""**"
"7119","Umm Anas رضي الله عنها said: O Messenger of Allah, enjoin me. He ﷺ said: > **""Abandon sins, for that is the best emigration. Guard the obligations, for that is the best jihād. And increase in remembrance of Allah, for you will bring to Allah nothing more beloved to Him than His remembrance.""**"
"7120","Muʿādh رضي الله عنه said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, enjoin me. He ﷺ said: > **""Worship Allah as though you see Him, count yourself among the dead, remember Allah at every stone and at every tree, and when you do an evil deed then do beside it a good deed: a secret one for a secret one, and an open one for an open one.""**"
"7121","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Guarantee me six from yourselves and I shall guarantee you Paradise: be truthful when you speak, fulfill when you promise, render when you are entrusted, guard your private parts, lower your gazes, and restrain your hands.""**"
"7122","Abū Kāhil رضي الله عنه said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, shall I tell you of a decree Allah has taken upon Himself, then supplicated life for my heart on the day my body dies. He ﷺ then detailed its counsels on fear of Allah, veiling faults, sweetness of prayer, congregation, fasting, restraining harm, dutifulness to parents living and dead by seeking forgiveness for them and never reviling them nor others' parents, paying zakāt, providing from the lawful, sending blessings upon him ﷺ, and testimony of unity, and said: > **""Know, O Abū Kāhil, that whoever testifies that none is worthy of worship but Allah alone, certain of it, it is binding upon Allah to forgive him with each utterance the sins of a year.""**"
"7123","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما said: we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a Bedouin in a brocaded cloak claimed the Prophet ﷺ debases nobles and raises shepherds. The Prophet ﷺ seized his cloak and reproached his dress, then narrated the will of Nūḥ عليه السلام to his son with two commands and two prohibitions, and explained pride when asked about fine sandals, garments, mounts, and companions, saying: > **""Pride is contempt for the truth and despising people.""**"
"7124","In another narration from him رضي الله عنه: a Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ in a Ṭayālisah cloak wrapped with brocade. The Prophet ﷺ then sat and said that Nūḥ عليه السلام at death called his two sons and shortened the will to two commands and two prohibitions, forbidding shirk and pride and commanding Lā ilāha illallāh which outweighs the heavens, earth, and what is between them, and adding: > **""And I enjoin upon you glorification, for it is the worship of creation, and magnification.""**"
"7125","Al-Agharr Abū Mālik said: when Abū Bakr رضي الله عنه intended to appoint ʿUmar رضي الله عنه as successor, he summoned him and said, I call you to a matter burdensome for whoever undertakes it, so fear Allah O ʿUmar through obeying Him and obey Him through fearing Him, for piety is a safeguarded matter. Whoever commands truth yet acts with falsehood, and commands good yet acts with evil, his hope will soon be cut and his deed will encompass him. If you govern them, keep your hand dry of their blood, your belly empty of their wealth, and your tongue restrained from their honor, if you are able, then do so, and there is no might nor power except through Allah."
"7126","Abū Rāfiʿ said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه leaned upon Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما with Ibn ʿUmar and Saʿīd ibn Zayd رضي الله عنهم present, and said, know I have decreed nothing on Kalālah, I appoint no successor after me, and whoever of the Arab captives lives to my death is free from the wealth of Allah. When Saʿīd suggested naming a man as Abū Bakr had done, ʿUmar said he had seen blameworthy eagerness among his companions, so he entrusts the matter to the six with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died pleased. Had Sālim freedman of Abū Ḥudhayfah or Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ رضي الله عنهم lived, he would have entrusted it to him with confidence."
"7127","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: I was the first to reach ʿUmar رضي الله عنه when he was stabbed. He said, retain three from me, for I fear people will not reach me: I passed no judgment on Kalālah, I appoint no caliph over people, and every slave of mine is free."
"7128","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: al-ʿAbbās رضي الله عنه said to me, O my son, the Commander of the Believers summons you, draws you near, and consults you with the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so retain three traits from me: beware he ever detects a lie from you, never divulge his secret, and never backbite anyone before him. ʿĀmir said to Ibn ʿAbbās, each is better than a thousand, and he replied, each is better than ten thousand."
"7129","Saʿd رضي الله عنه said to his son at death: O my son, you will meet none more sincere to you than me. When you intend prayer, perfect your ablution, then pray a prayer as though you will not pray after it. Beware of greed, for it is present poverty; upon you is despair of what people hold, for that is richness. Beware of any deed or word requiring apology, and do besides that as seems to you."
"7130","Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn said: a man with his companions came to Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه greeting him and supplicating for him. Muʿādh said, I enjoin you with two matters: if you guard them you are guarded. You cannot do without your share of this world, yet you are needier of your share of the Hereafter, so prefer your share of the Hereafter over your share of this world until it orders it for you in full order, then it departs with you wherever you go."
"7131","ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Suwayd al-Minqarī said: I witnessed Qays ibn ʿĀṣim رضي الله عنه enjoining his thirty-two sons. He said, O my sons, when I die make your eldest your chief to succeed your father, and do not make your youngest chief lest that debase you before your peers. Set no wailing woman over me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid wailing. Tend wealth, for it awakens the noble and frees from need of the base. Spend camels only in their right and withhold not their right. Beware every evil stock, for what delights you one day will grieve you more. Beware the sons of your enemies, for they are enemies upon the way of their fathers. When I die bury me where the tribe of Bakr ibn Wāʾil cannot discover, for there were violent feuds between us in Jāhiliyyah, and I fear they will exhume me and ruin their world and your Hereafter. Then he called for his quiver and commanded his eldest son ʿAlī to break one arrow, then two, which he broke, then thirty bound with a bowstring, which he could not break. He said, O my sons, thus you are in unity and thus in division, then recited verses on glory built by a truthful father and kept alive by the child, on thirty sons bound like arrows against calamities, on giving leadership to elders, and on guarding the young until the strained youngest reaches maturity."
